{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HoefsmitV21CosSymmetrization","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HoefsmitV21CosSymmetrization","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Matrix.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Inverse","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":27,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.eigenphase_forced","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.eigenphase_forced","kind":"theorem","line":334,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HoefsmitV21CosSymmetrization.lean#L334-L343","doc":"**Eigenphase forcing.** A real `2×2` rotation (`det = 1`,\n`|trace| ≤ 2`) has its trace pinned to `2 cos θ` at the forced angle\n`θ = arccos(trace/2)`: concretely `2 · cos(arccos(t/2)) = t` for\n`|t| ≤ 2`. The provable kinematic core of the Borromean spectral\nphase `θ = arccos(χ^(2,1)(𝓑₃)/2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_V21_cos_symmetrization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_V21_cos_symmetrization","kind":"theorem","line":276,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HoefsmitV21CosSymmetrization.lean#L276-L306","doc":"**Hoefsmit V_(2,1) cos symmetrization (canonical export).** Bundles the\nHoefsmit matrix definitions, the Hecke quadratic identity on BOTH\nσ_0 (diagonal) and σ_1 (off-diagonal), the trace + determinant\nclosed forms for σ_1, and the Markov-symmetrized character closed\nform on V_(2,1). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:hoefsmit-V21-cos-symmetrization","label":"prop:hoefsmit-V21-cos-symmetrization","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-V21-cos-symmetrization.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_V21_symmetrization_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_V21_symmetrization_even","kind":"theorem","line":266,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HoefsmitV21CosSymmetrization.lean#L266-L271","doc":"The symmetrization is even in the eigenphase (cos is even). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_V21_markov_symmetrized_character","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_V21_markov_symmetrized_character","kind":"theorem","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HoefsmitV21CosSymmetrization.lean#L257-L264","doc":"**Markov-symmetrized V_(2,1) character (closed form).** Under the\neigenphase axiomatisation, the symmetrized character equals the\nunsymmetrized matrix-trace character times `cos((z-1) h / 2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.markovSymmetrizedV21Character","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.markovSymmetrizedV21Character","kind":"def","line":248,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HoefsmitV21CosSymmetrization.lean#L248-L253","doc":"The Markov-symmetrized V_(2,1) character of a typed braid is\nobtained by multiplying its unsymmetrized matrix-trace character\nby `cos((z-1) h / 2)`. This is the canonical functional, not a\nuniversally-quantified existence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.V21Eigenphase.cos_bar_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.V21Eigenphase.cos_bar_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HoefsmitV21CosSymmetrization.lean#L238-L238","doc":"Cos of the eigenphase is bar-invariant (`q ↔ q⁻¹`). This is the\nbar-symmetry constraint on the Markov-trace symmetrization,\nforced by the cyclic property `τ(σ_i x) = τ(x σ_i)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.V21Eigenphase.symmetrized_character_bounded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.V21Eigenphase.symmetrized_character_bounded","kind":"theorem","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HoefsmitV21CosSymmetrization.lean#L233-L233","doc":"The Markov-traced V_(2,1) character on a typed braid at single\nwrap equals `2 · cos(eigenphase q)`. Concrete consequence: the\nsymmetrized character has magnitude bounded by 2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.V21Eigenphase.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.V21Eigenphase.mk","kind":"ctor","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HoefsmitV21CosSymmetrization.lean#L229-L229","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.V21Eigenphase","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.V21Eigenphase","kind":"class","line":220,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HoefsmitV21CosSymmetrization.lean#L220-L239","doc":"**Hoefsmit V_(2,1) eigenphase axiomatisation**: the transfer-matrix\nspectrum on V_(2,1) is `{e^{+i·eigenphase q}, e^{-i·eigenphase q}}`.\n\nEstablished at the combinatorial level in\n`prop:beta-decay-transfer-matrix`; we record it here as a class\nfield since the underlying eigenvalue computation lives in the\nexisting Python infrastructure\n(`computations/hecke_characters.build_seminormal_matrices`)\nand is not yet machine-proved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.eigenphase","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.eigenphase","kind":"def","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HoefsmitV21CosSymmetrization.lean#L217-L218","doc":"The single-wrap eigenphase on V_(2,1): `α = (z - 1) h / 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.heckeH","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.heckeH","kind":"def","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HoefsmitV21CosSymmetrization.lean#L214-L215","doc":"Quantum-integer differential. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.markovZ_legacy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.markovZ_legacy","kind":"def","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HoefsmitV21CosSymmetrization.lean#L208-L212","doc":"**Legacy unsafe form** of `cosKernel` — `Real.sqrt q` without the\n`0 < q` hypothesis. Use `cosKernel (u : R)` (Tier 2) or `markovZ_real\nq hq` (Tier 5) in new code. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.markovZ_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.markovZ_real","kind":"def","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HoefsmitV21CosSymmetrization.lean#L196-L206","doc":"Archimedean shim of `cosKernel` with explicit positivity.\n\n**Convention D** `z_D q = q³/(q²+1) = q² · (kernel at q)`, migrated from\nconvention C 2026-08-26 (bean `qou-cxjq`). This read `(kernel at √q)`, i.e.\n`√q/(q+1)`. The rescaled shape is the only one available: no argument\nreaches D (`no_kernel_instantiation_is_conventionD`); see\n`QOU.BraidKnot.markovZD_eq_sq_mul_kernel`. The `0 < q` hypothesis is kept for\nAPI compatibility and is now genuinely unused — convention D has no\n`Real.sqrt` in it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.cosKernel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.cosKernel","kind":"def","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HoefsmitV21CosSymmetrization.lean#L184-L194","doc":"Markov-Jones parameter (Tier 2 / generic-R form):\n`z = u / (u² + 1) = 1 / (u + u⁻¹)`.\n\n**This is the KERNEL, not a Markov parameter — convention-C shaped, kept\ndeliberately** (bean `qou-cxjq`, 2026-08-26). It is convention-neutral *as a\nfunction*; the convention lives in how it is instantiated. Convention D is\n**not** this at any argument — `QOU.BraidKnot.no_kernel_instantiation_is_conventionD`\nproves the kernel's real range is `[-1/2, 1/2]` while `z_D q > 1/2` for every\n`q > 1` — it is the rescaling `q² · (this kernel at q)`. Consume the `_real`\nshim below, which is convention D. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_sigma1_hecke_quadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_sigma1_hecke_quadratic","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HoefsmitV21CosSymmetrization.lean#L154-L176","doc":"σ_1's off-diagonal action squares to the Hecke quadratic identity at the\nmatrix level: `M² = (q − q⁻¹) · M + I`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_sigma1_det_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_sigma1_det_eq","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HoefsmitV21CosSymmetrization.lean#L140-L152","doc":"Determinant of σ_1: `det(σ_1) = d_1·d_2 − b² = −1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_sigma1_trace_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_sigma1_trace_eq","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HoefsmitV21CosSymmetrization.lean#L129-L138","doc":"Trace of σ_1: `tr(σ_1) = d_1 + d_2 = q − q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_b_sq_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_b_sq_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HoefsmitV21CosSymmetrization.lean#L121-L127","doc":"`b² ≥ 0` (so `sqrt(b²)² = b²` cleanly). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_b_sq_closed_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_b_sq_closed_form","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HoefsmitV21CosSymmetrization.lean#L113-L119","doc":"Auxiliary closed form: `b² = (q⁴ + q² + 1) / (q² + 1)²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_sigma0_hecke_quadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_sigma0_hecke_quadratic","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HoefsmitV21CosSymmetrization.lean#L84-L100","doc":"σ_0's diagonal action squares to the Hecke quadratic identity at the\nmatrix level: `M^2 = (q - q⁻¹) M + I`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_sigma1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_sigma1","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HoefsmitV21CosSymmetrization.lean#L70-L75","doc":"Backward-compatibility alias — `hoefsmit_sigma1` is the legacy form.\nPhase 2 migrates the file's theorems to use `hoefsmit_sigma1_gen`\ndirectly; until then, this alias keeps existing references compiling. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_sigma1_legacy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_sigma1_legacy","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HoefsmitV21CosSymmetrization.lean#L60-L68","doc":"**Legacy archimedean form** of `hoefsmit_sigma1` — instantiates the\noff-diagonal as `Real.sqrt (hoefsmit_b_sq q)` without an explicit\n`0 ≤ hoefsmit_b_sq q` hypothesis. Kept for backward compatibility\nwith the existing theorems in this file; new code should use the\ngeneric `hoefsmit_sigma1_gen` with an explicit square-root witness. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_sigma1_gen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_sigma1_gen","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HoefsmitV21CosSymmetrization.lean#L47-L58","doc":"Hoefsmit ρ_(2,1)(σ_1) 2x2 matrix — **Tier 2 generic-R form**.\nThe off-diagonal entry `b` is taken as an abstract square-root of\n`hoefsmit_b_sq q`; downstream consumers supply the witness either\nformally (`u² = q` style adjoin) or archimedeanly (`Real.sqrt` with\na positivity hypothesis on `hoefsmit_b_sq q`).\n\nMathematically: `b² = hoefsmit_b_sq q` is the Hecke quadratic\nconstraint; this constructor leaves the choice of square-root\nrepresentative to the caller. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_sigma0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_sigma0","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HoefsmitV21CosSymmetrization.lean#L43-L45","doc":"The Hoefsmit ρ_(2,1)(σ_0) 2x2 matrix — diagonal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_b_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_b_sq","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HoefsmitV21CosSymmetrization.lean#L39-L41","doc":"Off-diagonal coupling square `b^2 = d_1 · d_2 + 1` (Hecke quadratic\nconstraint on σ_1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_d2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_d2","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HoefsmitV21CosSymmetrization.lean#L36-L37","doc":"Hoefsmit diagonal `d_2` entry of `ρ_(2,1)(σ_1)`: `-q⁻¹ / (q^2 + 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_d1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hoefsmit_d1","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HoefsmitV21CosSymmetrization.lean#L33-L34","doc":"Hoefsmit diagonal `d_1` entry of `ρ_(2,1)(σ_1)`: `q^3 / (q^2 + 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}